--
-- What this Part is. Section 1175 is shown as dots (repealed or blank in this text). Sections 1176 to 1180 amend or
-- repeal provisions of the Companies Act 1985 and the Companies Act 1989 and save proceedings begun before the
-- commencement of s 1176: amendments of other Acts and a saving that affects no one now, inert under reason 2
-- (machinery) in NOTES.md. Section 1181 is an order-making power over the Leasehold Reform, Housing and Urban
-- Development Act 1993 and the Commonhold and Leasehold Reform Act 2002 (machinery, inert); the two defined terms of
-- s 1181(4) are the only definitions in this Part and are encoded here.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; NOTES.md, "Reading a result").
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words: -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<quoted words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide: -- NOTHING-kind (<why>)
-- Every name below begins with the section label it implements.

§ `Part 39: companies, minor amendments`

